IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-dates`
IMPORT `sda-work`

-- Sex Discrimination Act 1984 (Cth), baseline 2026-11 -- worked cases for the questions that take a few facts each:
-- ss 28A, 28AA, 28M, 47A, 94, 110, and AHRC Act ss 46P, 46PH(1)(b), 46PO(2), 46PSA.
-- Every expected value was written by hand from the text; the comment on each gives the provision. The facts are
-- HYPOTHETICAL.

§ `Cases with a few facts`

§§ `s 28A`

-- an unwelcome request for sexual favours that a reasonable person would see might offend
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- a sexual remark made in my presence (s 28A(2): a statement of a sexual nature in the presence of a person)
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- unwelcome, but a reasonable person would not have anticipated offence, humiliation or intimidation
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I sexually harassed` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- nothing sexual and unwelcome
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I sexually harassed` FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `s 28AA`

-- demeaning comments about women's competence, made to me because I am a woman
#ASSERT `Was I harassed on the ground of my sex` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- demeaning, but not by reason of sex or a characteristic of my sex
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I harassed on the ground of my sex` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- the reasonable-person limb fails
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I harassed on the ground of my sex` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `s 28M`

-- on 13 December 2022, the day s 28M commenced: a hostile environment where I work
#ASSERT `Was I subjected to a hostile workplace environment` (`the date` 13 12 2022) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- the same on 12 December 2022, before s 28M existed
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I subjected to a hostile workplace environment` (`the date` 12 12 2022) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- in a workplace where only the person who did it works, and I came in afterwards (s 28M(2)(a), (b))
#ASSERT `Was I subjected to a hostile workplace environment` (`the date` 1 6 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- I was never in the workplace at the time or after
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I subjected to a hostile workplace environment` (`the date` 1 6 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- the reasonable-person limb fails
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I subjected to a hostile workplace environment` (`the date` 1 6 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- not in a workplace where either of us works
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I subjected to a hostile workplace environment` (`the date` 1 6 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `s 47A`

-- demoted after complaining of harassment
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `victimisation, unlawful under s 47A`
-- detriment only for an allegation proved false and not made in good faith (s 47A(3))
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the s 47A(3) defence applies: the allegation was false and not made in good faith`
-- no detriment for speaking up
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not victimisation under s 47A`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not victimisation under s 47A`

§§ `s 94`

-- an individual: 25 penalty units or 3 months, or both
#ASSERT `What is the most they can be fined in penalty units` FALSE EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `What is the longest they can be imprisoned in months` FALSE EQUALS 3
-- a body corporate: 100 penalty units, no imprisonment
#ASSERT `What is the most they can be fined in penalty units` TRUE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `What is the longest they can be imprisoned in months` TRUE EQUALS 0

§§ `s 110`

-- no complaint or claim of one's own for a breach of s 47C as such
#ASSERT NOT `Can I bring my own claim for a breach of the positive duty`

§§ `AHRC Act s 46P`

-- a written, arguable complaint of harassment by the person harassed
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commission` `conduct unlawful under Part II (discrimination, harassment, a hostile workplace or victimisation)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- a complaint only that the employer failed in the positive duty: Part IIA is not "unlawful discrimination" (s 3(1)(c))
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I complain to the Commission` `only a failure of the positive duty (Part IIA)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- not in writing
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I complain to the Commission` `conduct unlawful under Part II (discrimination, harassment, a hostile workplace or victimisation)` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- not reasonably arguable (s 46P(1A))
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I complain to the Commission` `conduct unlawful under Part II (discrimination, harassment, a hostile workplace or victimisation)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- lodged by a trade union on my behalf (s 46P(2)(c))
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commission` `conduct unlawful under Part II (discrimination, harassment, a hostile workplace or victimisation)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- already a class member of a representative complaint about the same subject matter (s 46P(3))
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I complain to the Commission` `conduct unlawful under Part II (discrimination, harassment, a hostile workplace or victimisation)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b)`

-- lodged exactly 24 months after: not "more than 24 months"
#ASSERT NOT (`May the President end my complaint because it is late` (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 3 2026))
-- one day later
#ASSERT `May the President end my complaint because it is late` (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 2 3 2026)
-- well within time
#ASSERT NOT (`May the President end my complaint because it is late` (`the date` 1 3 2024) (`the date` 1 1 2025))
-- conduct on 29 February 2024: 24 months on is read as 28 February 2026 (finding 9), so 1 March 2026 is late
#ASSERT NOT (`May the President end my complaint because it is late` (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 28 2 2026))
#ASSERT `May the President end my complaint because it is late` (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 1 3 2026)

§§ `AHRC Act s 46PO(2)`

-- notice issued 1 March 2026: 30 days to 31 March, 60 days to 30 April 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to the court` (`the date` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `the date` 30 4 2026
-- notice issued 15 December 2025: 16 days to 31 December, 47 to 31 January, 60 days to 13 February 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to the court` (`the date` 15 12 2025) EQUALS `the date` 13 2 2026

§§ `AHRC Act s 46PSA`

-- I lose to a respondent with no power or resources advantage (s 46PSA(6)(c))
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- I lose to my employer, which has a significant power advantage: s 46PSA(5) protects me
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- I lose to a respondent with significantly greater resources only
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- vexatious proceedings, whoever the respondent (s 46PSA(6)(a))
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- my unreasonable act caused their costs (s 46PSA(6)(b))
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- the respondent did not win and none of (6) applies
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- I win on one ground: the respondent must be ordered to pay my costs (s 46PSA(2))
#ASSERT `Must the respondent pay my costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the respondent must be ordered to pay my costs`
-- I win, but my own unreasonable act caused some of my costs (s 46PSA(4))
#ASSERT `Must the respondent pay my costs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the respondent must be ordered to pay my costs, except those my own unreasonable act or omission caused`
-- I do not succeed on any ground
#ASSERT `Must the respondent pay my costs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 46PSA(2) does not apply: I did not succeed on any ground`
